Mathesis Reader · Μάθησις Στοιχείων

The code in this repository is MIT and the app's own writing is CC BY-SA 4.0 (see LICENSE).
This file lists the material from other sources that the app shows, its licence, and what the app
changes in it. The app's Credits page (src/app/credits/page.tsx) gives the same list, with links.
None of this material is copied into the repository: the app reads it, when it is needed, from the
old site (https://mathesisstoicheion.com/data/ and /packs/) and from GitHub. The test fixtures in
test-fixtures/ and src/lib/lookup/fixtures/ are unchanged copies kept for the automated tests only.


TEXTS AND TRANSLATIONS

Shown exactly as published, never edited. The catalogue (the old site's data/catalog.json) is built
from these collections, each pinned to one commit:

- Perseus Digital Library, Tufts University: canonical-greekLit (PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit,
  commit bcc5df0602f3b3fe6fefe1e1d575602a25ab1db6). CC BY-SA 4.0. doi:10.5281/zenodo.596309.
  Perseus asks that any modifications be offered back to Perseus.
- Open Greek and Latin, First Thousand Years of Greek (OpenGreekAndLatin/First1KGreek,
  commit 8ee111eb44ecef4120c844e10749178d95d1f30c). CC BY-SA 4.0. doi:10.5281/zenodo.596723.
- The editor and translator of each text, as named in that text file's header.


WORDS AND DICTIONARIES

- GLAUx, by Alek Keersmaekers: word analyses, sentence structure, and each work's genre.
  CC BY-SA 4.0; some source texts and hand annotations inside GLAUx carry other licences, listed in
  GLAUx's metadata. Keersmaekers, A. (2021), "The GLAUx corpus: methodological issues in designing a
  long-term, diverse, multi-layered corpus of Ancient Greek", Proceedings of the 2nd International
  Workshop on Computational Approaches to Historical Language Change, 39-50.
- Liddell-Scott-Jones Greek-English Lexicon (LSJ): Text provided under a CC BY-SA license by Perseus
  Digital Library, http://www.perseus.tufts.edu, with funding from The National Endowment for the
  Humanities. Data accessed from https://github.com/PerseusDL/lexica/.
- Dickinson College Commentaries Greek Core Vocabulary, by Christopher Francese and collaborators.
  CC BY-SA 3.0.
- Wikidata (authors' Greek names, other names, occupations and descriptions). CC0.


