WHAT THIS APP CHANGES

As CC BY-SA asks, the changes made to the material above:
- Texts are split into citable passages and lined up with their translations. Their words are not
  changed. Text is drawn in Unicode's composed form (NFC), which is the same text: a letter that a
  file writes as a base letter and a separate mark is drawn as the one letter it is.
- LSJ entries keep their wording; Beta Code is turned into Greek letters, and a short gloss is taken
  from each entry for the look-up (both done by the old site's pipeline).
- Works are grouped by kind of writing, from GLAUx's genres and Wikidata's occupations.
- Wikidata's descriptions are shown with BCE and CE written as BC and AD.
